  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Who does the action",
   "texto": [
    "The active participle of present is formed from imperfect verbs. A practical track is the 3rd plural person: **читать — читают — читающий**. According to the conjugation, **-ущ-/-ющ-** or **-ащ-/-ящ-** appears.",
    "Concords with the noun in gender, number and case: **читающий человек**, **вижу читающего человека**, **о читающем человеке**. The noun is the one who does the action.",
    "«Presente» indicates that part of the base is not passed and expresses a simultaneous action with that of the main verb; it does not necessarily mean «Now». Not all imperfect verbs have a natural participle."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Equivalence with «который»",
   "texto": [
    "You can replace a relative with **который**: **человек, читающий газету** = **человек, который читает газету**.",
    "If the participial phrase goes after the noun, it is usually separated with coma; if it goes ahead, it is not usually **читающий газету человек**. In conversation, **который** is usually preferred."
   ]
  },
